# Strategies

Each strategy is an independent pure plug-in. It consumes an immutable
`FeatureSnapshot` and a read-only portfolio view, and returns zero or more
`TradeIntent` objects.

## Prohibited

- Broker calls, OMS access, order construction, final quantity.
- Reading mutable global state or a partially updated feature frame.
- Calling another strategy, forming a pipeline.
- LLM or network calls of any kind.
- Naked short options.

## Required

- Pure function of its inputs. Same snapshot and config yields the same intents.
- A complete exit template on every intent: stop, target, time, expiry,
  invalidation, and a multi-leg partial-fill policy.
- A deterministic path when no promoted AI proposal is available: approved
  baseline or abstain. Missing or expired proposal is never an error.
- Confidence is evidence, not permission. A high score cannot substitute for a
  failed hard gate.

## Specifications

One spec per strategy, from `docs/context/STRATEGY_SPECS/TEMPLATE.md`. Do not
invent production defaults; leave parameters unset until research sets them and
record every trial. Preserve a final holdout.

Follow roadmap order. CAS and microstructure are Phase 7, not early work.
